  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 600.65 K, melting point of Pb; 1.147 kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 8.880 + 0.116 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.471 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=8.880\\times10^{-3}T+0.058\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.471\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.811$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-600.65 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 16.171 - 0.142 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 1.866 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 54.350 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta \\mathrm{Gr}^{\\circ} = 16.171 + 0.142 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 1.866 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 27.175 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 19.080 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \n600.65-2000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = 15.823 - 2.706 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 0.111 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 70.950 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = 15.823 + 2.706 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 0.111 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 35.475 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 33.741 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Chase (18). ",
